CORE gcc-only no-new-smt
arm.c
--arch arm --unwind 3
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 19 teq/bne loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 32 cmp/bne loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.unwind\.0\] line 37 unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line 48 store in the loop: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
^\[main\.unwind\.1\]
--
The retry loops of load-exclusive/store-exclusive sequences that end with
teq or cmp of the status and bne need no unwinding; a loop whose attempts
store to memory remains a loop. The assertion that fails may be violated on
hardware, where a store-exclusive may fail spuriously.
